_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.4756851571892967,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.010348928958242931,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":60.3,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.030554117029952144,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":11.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.16873699313625376,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.19629999,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.091,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":9.1,"pf":[],"description_full":"Sight Sciences, Inc., an ophthalmic medical device company, focuses on the development and commercialization of surgical and nonsurgical technologies for the treatment of eye prevalent diseases in the United States. The company operates in two segments, Surgical Glaucoma and Dry Eye. It offers OMNI, a surgical system family of products, such as OMNI Ergo for the catheterization and transluminal viscodilation of Schlemm's canal and cutting of the trabecular meshwork to reduce intraocular pressure in adult patients with open-angle glaucoma; and OMNI EDGE, an implant-free and minimally invasive glaucoma surgery technology. The company also provides SION, a bladeless and manually operated device used in ophthalmic surgical procedures to excise trabecular meshwork; and TearCare system, a proprietary, interventional, dry eye device designed to melt and facilitate the comprehensive removal of meibomian gland obstructions and restore gland functionality and healthy oil production for adult patients with evaporative dry eye disease due to meibomian gland disease when used in conjunction with manual expression of the meibomian glands for ophthalmologists and optometrists. It serves hospitals, medical centers, and eyecare professionals through sales representatives and distributors. The company was incorporated in 2010 and is headquartered in Menlo Park, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Paul  Badawi | Co-Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 186 people. Revenue per employee of $416K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $70K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Sight Sciences, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $602M market cap on $77M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at -469% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 85% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $30M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -7.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 17% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 48% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3793355239138369},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (91% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.091},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 313% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Healthcare peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Financial Contrast: Sight Sciences (NASDAQ:SGHT) vs. Pulmonx (NASDAQ:LUNG)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/financial-contrast-sight-sciences-nasdaqsght-vs-pulmonx-nasdaqlung.html","date":"202